<figure class="crf-follower-figure" aria-labelledby="follower-title" data-safe-follower>
 <figcaption><span class="crf-number">Figure 3</span><span id="follower-title">When can the nearby follower answer at T?</span></figcaption>
 <div class="crf-frame">
  <div class="crf-request">SQL gateway requests <strong>one timestamp T</strong><span>for every range this read touches</span></div>
  <div class="crf-replicas">
   <div class="crf-replica"><p class="crf-label">P7 range · leaseholder</p><div class="crf-log"><span>…</span><span>command k</span><span>…</span></div><p>The promise: no new writes at or below T.</p></div>
   <div class="crf-replica"><p class="crf-label">Same range · nearby follower</p><div class="crf-evidence"><span>Closed through T</span><strong data-closed data-live>not received</strong><span>Applied through k</span><strong data-applied data-live>not yet</strong></div><p class="crf-verdict" data-verdict data-live>Cannot answer T locally</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="crf-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The follower has an older P7 version. That alone does not tell it whether a missing write belongs before T.</p>
  <div class="crf-controls" role="group" aria-label="Follower safety playback"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div><div class="crf-hold" data-hold><span></span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="crf-caption">A conceptual range-level model, with symbolic timestamp T and replication position k. The follower needs the closing promise and the replication history associated with it. No particular node placement, traffic or elapsed time is measured here.</p>
 <details><summary>Read the safety test as text</summary><ol><li>An old version alone is insufficient.</li><li>The follower receives a promise closing T, tied to replication position k.</li><li>It has not yet applied through k, so it still cannot serve T.</li><li>After applying through k it has the history needed at T. A read spanning several ranges must qualify each range at the same timestamp.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-safe-follower]')){
 const text=(selector:string,value:string)=>{root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=value};
 const explanations=['The follower has an older P7 version. That alone does not tell it whether a missing write belongs before T.','The leaseholder closes T and associates that promise with replication position k. The promise says no new write can enter this range at or below T.','The follower has the closing promise, but it is still applying earlier commands. A missing command could change its answer at T.','The follower has applied through k as well. It can now serve this range at T. Other ranges needed by the query must be safe at the same T.'];
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(step:number)=>{text('[data-closed]',step>=1?'received, tied to k':'not received');text('[data-applied]',step>=3?'yes':'not yet');text('[data-verdict]',step>=3?'Can serve this range at T':'Cannot answer T locally');text('[data-explanation]',explanations[step]);root.querySelector('.crf-verdict')!.classList.toggle('safe',step>=3)}});
}
</script>
